  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "Database updates and new fusion and chimeric RNA methods give cancer RNA-seq more curated context and fewer false-positive transcript calls.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure for interpreting cancer transcriptomes, split between curated resources and transcript-level discovery. LncRNAfunc 2.0 integrates TCGA, GTEx, CCLE, binding and perturbation evidence for cancer lncRNAs, and iGPSC-DB catalogs inferred single-cell genetic perturbation effects. R-loopBase v2.0 reanalyses 358 datasets from 16 technologies with quantitative confidence scoring across four species. On the discovery side, RIFTT combines Arriba and FusionCatcher with new scoring metrics to reduce fusion false positives, benchmarked on TCGA-LAML and BeatAML. An integrative pipeline reports 569,640 chimeric RNAs across 1019 cancer cell lines and links candidates to cell fitness through dependency screening. TailEnrich, a preprint, tests expression distribution tails for disease-sample enrichment to find subset-specific dysregulated genes. The stem.MAP preprint on protein complexes in embryonic stem cells is peripheral to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
